! mcp_bootstrap_p300.strap -- MCP printed page 300: THE $TIME PSEUDO OP
! (Z TIME .. S TIME K), lines 1-47.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.51, read at 400 dpi.  Header, READ:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID QK000001  DIST. OF 3/01
! 3/01  PAGE NUMBER 300" (round glyphs in numeric fields read 0; the Q of
! QK prints open like C, the serials print a clear QK).  The heading
! row's LOCATION field is BLANK.  CARD ID QK000001 -- a new card-ID
! series begins on this page.
!
! THE PAGE.  47 lines, every line number prints a "*" after it.  Lines
! 1-7 are remark cards (a banner "****** THE $TIME PSEUDO OP ******"
! between two rows of asterisks; "CALLING SEQUENCE / B,$MCP ,$TIME
! ,FWA(I)").  Line 8 "SLC,$" prints 233107.00 and a "*"; this deck
! restates it as a hard SLC (as p.297 does).  Located rows run
! contiguous from 233107.00 (line 9) to 233143.00 (line 47, S TIME K
! VF,0.0, printed 000000.00+), then blank paper.  "*" after the
! LOCATION on lines 8, 25 and 37.
!
! JOIN.  p.299 has no scratch neighbour; contiguity with it is NOT
! established here (p.297 ended at 233003.00).  This page's labels match
! the landed forward references: p.178 B,ZTIME -> 233107.10 (ZTIME at
! 233107.00, line 9); p.146/p.178 stand-ins ZT8 233136.0 and ZT81
! 233141.0 (here lines 38 and 43).  p.301 should open at 233143.40.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * "Z TIME", "Z T 1", "Z T 2", "Z T8", "Z T8 1", "Z T 9", "S TIME K",
!     "S T LR", "K SUPP", "S FORBD": spaces are the drum's; spellings as
!     landed (ZTIME p.178, ZT8/ZT81 p.146/p.178, STLR, KSUPP, SFORBD).
!   * line 33 "ST(CU,63,8)": D with a worn stem -- the second half prints
!     077000.24, the decimal-mode bit, so DU (as p.297 lines 39/41).
!   * line 46 "B,SCISP" = SDISP (worn D; landed SDISP 217372.0, binary
!     217372.10).
!   * line 15 "LVE,1,C.O", line 47 "VF,C.O", lines 26/31 "0.2C($1)",
!     line 34 "(2)C1110101", line 35/36 "C.16"/"C.40": open round glyphs
!     in numeric fields read 0.
!   * octal fields "CCCCCC.CC" read 0; hex "CO", "FO", "DO" = C0, F0, D0.
!     Line 24's second byte prints "DC"; line 27 (the same statement)
!     prints "D0" -- read D0.  Line 28's "BC" read B0.
!   * line 19 remark "-TC CHECK BOUNDS" -- TO with the open O.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  QK000001 .. QK000045.  Lines 1-18 print QK0000NN; line
! 19 ALSO prints QK000018; lines 20-45 print QK0000(N-1); line 46 ALSO
! prints QK000044; line 47 prints QK000045.  Two duplicated serials,
! none skipped.  Recorded, not explained.

STIC    SYN(B,25,1), (8)215265.0     ! landed; p.116 line 16 STIC VF,0
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0             ! landed; p.116 line 13 DRZ(BU,64),29
SL      SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.04      ! p.103 line 14 -LEVEL OF INSTR
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0             ! p.128 line 3 "K SUPP NOP,K COMM R"
SFORBD  SYN,(16)1009.0               ! p.107 line 14 - 9 COMMUNICATION WITH
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! landed; SIC, BIT-EXACT
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! landed; B, half word only

        SLC, (8)233107.00
! line  1  - ******************************************************
! line  2  - ****** THE $TIME PSEUDO OP ******
